#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qiskit.primitives\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "qiskit.primitives {#qiskitprimitives}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most notable change in the [`qiskit.primitives`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/primitives) module is the\n"
"introduction of the new **primitives V2 interface**. This section shows how to migrate your\n"
"workflow from primitives V1 to primitives V2, as well as the few changes that have taken place\n"
"in the inputs accepted by the V1 interface.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Starting with the v1.0 release, we will refer to the pre-1.0 primitives interface as \"primitives V1\".\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"migrate-to-v2\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from V1 to V2 {#migrate-from-v1-to-v2}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The formal distinction between the primitives V1 and V2 APIs are the base classes from which\n"
"primitives implementations inherit. To transition to the new base classes, you can maintain\n"
"the original import path from `qiskit.primitives`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrate from                     |   Replace with\n"
"---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------\n"
"`BaseEstimator`         |  [`BaseEstimatorV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BaseEstimatorV2)\n"
"`BaseSampler`             |  [`BaseSamplerV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BaseSamplerV2)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The names of the qiskit core implementations of the V2 primitives (those importable from `qiskit.primitives`),\n"
"have been modified to clarify their purpose as implementations that can be run locally\n"
"with a statevector simulator backend. The new names **do not include the -V2 suffix**.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrate from                     |   Replace with\n"
"---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------\n"
"`qiskit.primitives.Estimator`         |  [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator)\n"
"`qiskit.primitives.Sampler`             |  [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are some conceptual differences to think about when migrating from V1 to V2.\n"
"These differences are dictated by the base class, but are shown in the following examples using the statevector\n"
"implementations found in `qiskit.primitives`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the following examples, assume the following imports and primitive "
"initializations:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1. `Sampler and Estimator`: The new V2 primitives are designed to accept **vectorized inputs**, where single circuits can be grouped with array-valued specifications. That is, one circuit can be executed\n"
"  for arrays of `n` parameter sets, `n` observables, or both (in the case of Estimator). Each group is called a **primitive unified bloc (pub)**, and can be represented as a tuple: `(1 x circuit, [n x observables], [n x parameters])`. The V1 interface didn't allow for the same flexibility.  Instead, the number of input circuits had to match the number of observables and\n"
"  parameter sets, as shown in the following examples (select a tab to see each example):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"e-1-4\" label=\"Estimator, 1 circuit, 4 observables\" default>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables using Estimator V1\n"
"      job = estimator_v1.run([circuit] * 4, [obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4])\n"
"      evs = job.result().values\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables using Estimator V2\n"
"      job = estimator_v2.run([(circuit, [obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4])])\n"
"      evs = job.result()[0].data.evs\n"
"      ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"s-1-3\" label=\"Sampler, 1 circuit, 3 parameter sets\" default>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 1 circuit with 3 parameter sets using Sampler V1\n"
"      job = sampler_v1.run([circuit] * 3, [vals1, vals2, vals3])\n"
"      dists = job.result().quasi_dists\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      # executing 1 circuit with 3 parameter sets using Sampler V2\n"
"      job = sampler_v2.run([(circuit, [vals1, vals2, vals3])])\n"
"      counts = job.result()[0].data.meas.get_counts()\n"
"      ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"e-1-4-2\" label=\"Estimator, 1 circuit, 4 observables, 2 parameter sets\" default>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables and 2 parameter sets using Estimator V1\n"
"      job = estimator_v1.run([circuit] * 8, [obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4] * 2, [vals1, vals2] * 4)\n"
"      evs = job.result().values\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      # executing 1 circuit with 4 observables and 2 parameter sets using Estimator V2\n"
"      job = estimator_v2.run([(circuit, [[obs1, obs2, obs3, obs4]], [[vals1], [vals2]])])\n"
"      evs = job.result()[0].data.evs\n"
"      ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  V2 primitives accept multiple PUBs as inputs, and each pub gets its own result. This\n"
"  lets you run different circuits with various parameter/observable combinations,\n"
"  which was not always possible in the V1 interface:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"s-2-1\" label=\"Sampler, 2 circuits, 1 parameter set\" default>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 2 circuits with 1 parameter set using Sampler V1\n"
"      job = sampler_v1.run([circuit1, circuit2], [vals1] * 2)\n"
"      dists = job.result().quasi_dists\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      # executing 2 circuits with 1 parameter set using Sampler V2\n"
"      job = sampler_v2.run([(circuit1, vals1), (circuit2, vals1)])\n"
"      counts1 = job.result()[0].data.meas.get_counts()  # result for pub 1 (circuit 1)\n"
"      counts2 = job.result()[1].data.meas.get_counts()  # result for pub 2 (circuit 2)\n"
"      ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"e-2-2\" label=\"Estimator, 2 circuits, 2 different observables\" default>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```python\n"
"      # executing 2 circuits with 2 different observables using Estimator V1\n"
"      job = estimator_v1.run([circuit1, circuit2] , [obs1, obs2])\n"
"      evs = job.result().values\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      # executing 2 circuits with 2 different observables using Estimator V2\n"
"      job = estimator_v2.run([(circuit1, obs1), (circuit2, obs2)])\n"
"      evs1 = job.result()[0].data.evs  # result for pub 1 (circuit 1)\n"
"      evs2 = job.result()[1].data.evs  # result for pub 2 (circuit 2)\n"
"      ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BaseSamplerV2): The V2 sampler now\n"
"returns measurement outcome samples in the form of **bitstrings** or\n"
"**counts**, instead of the quasi-probability distributions from the V1\n"
"interface. The bitstrings show the measurement outcomes, preserving the shot\n"
"order in which they were measured. The V2 Sampler result objects organize\n"
"data in terms of their input circuits' classical register names, for\n"
"compatibility with dynamic circuits.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    # Define quantum circuit with 2 qubits\n"
"    circuit = QuantumCircuit(2)\n"
"    circuit.h(0)\n"
"    circuit.cx(0, 1)\n"
"    circuit.measure_all()\n"
"    circuit.draw()\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```text\n"
"            ┌───┐      ░ ┌─┐\n"
"       q_0: ┤ H ├──■───░─┤M├───\n"
"            └───┘┌─┴─┐ ░ └╥┘┌─┐\n"
"       q_1: ─────┤ X ├─░──╫─┤M├\n"
"                 └───┘ ░  ║ └╥┘\n"
"    meas: 2/══════════════╩══╩═\n"
"                          0  1\n"
"    ```\n"
"    <Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Default classical register name\">\n"
"    In the circuit above, notice that the name of the classical register defaults to `\"meas\"`.\n"
"    This name will be used later to access the measurement bitstrings.\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    # Run using V1 Sampler\n"
"    result = sampler_v1.run(circuit).result()\n"
"    quasi_dist = result.quasi_dists[0]\n"
"    print(f\"The quasi-probability distribution is: {quasi_dist}\")\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```text\n"
"    The quasi-probability distribution is: {0: 0.5, 3: 0.5}\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    # Run using V2 Sampler\n"
"    result = sampler_v2.run([circuit]).result()\n"
"    # Access result data for pub 0\n"
"    data_pub = result[0].data\n"
"    # Access bitstrings for the classical register \"meas\"\n"
"    bitstrings = data_pub.meas.get_bitstrings()\n"
"    print(f\"The number of bitstrings is: {len(bitstrings)}\")\n"
"    # Get counts for the classical register \"meas\"\n"
"    counts = data_pub.meas.get_counts()\n"
"    print(f\"The counts are: {counts}\")\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```text\n"
"    The number of bitstrings is: 1024\n"
"    The counts are: {'00': 523, '11': 501}\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3. `Sampler and Estimator`: The sampling overhead, commonly exposed by V1 implementations\n"
"  through the `shots` run option, is now an argument of the primitives `run()` method\n"
"  that can be specified at the **PUB** level.\n"
"  The V2 base classes expose the arguments in formats different from the V1 API:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`BaseSamplerV2.run`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BaseSamplerV2#run)\n"
"exposes a `shots` argument (similar to the previous workflow):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        # Sample two circuits at 128 shots each.\n"
"        sampler_v2.run([circuit1, circuit2], shots=128)\n"
"        # Sample two circuits at different amounts of shots. \n"
"        # The \"None\"s are necessary as placeholders\n"
"        # for the lack of parameter values in this example.\n"
"        sampler_v2.run([(circuit1, None, 123), (circuit2, None, 456)])\n"
"        ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`EstimatorV2.run`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BaseEstimatorV2#run)\n"
"introduces a `precision` argument that specifies the error bars that the\n"
"primitive implementation should target for expectation values estimates:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        # Estimate expectation values for two PUBs, both with 0.05 precision.\n"
"        estimator_v2.run([(circuit1, obs_array1), \n"
"          (circuit2, obs_array_2)], precision=0.05\n"
"          )\n"
"        ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"v1-changes\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Updates in the V1 interface {#updates-in-the-v1-interface}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* Implicit conversion from a dense `BaseOperator` to a\n"
"  [`SparsePauliOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp) in\n"
"  [`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.primitives.Estimator) observable arguments\n"
"  is no longer allowed. You should explicitly convert to a `SparsePauliOp`\n"
"by using\n"
"  [`SparsePauliOp.from_operator(operator)`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp#from_operator)\n"
"  instead.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using a [`PauliList`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliList) in\n"
"Estimator observable arguments is no longer allowed. Instead you should\n"
"explicitly convert the argument by using\n"
"[`SparsePauliOp(pauli_list)`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp)\n"
"first.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qiskit.providers\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "qiskit.providers {#qiskitproviders}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"providers.basicaer\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "basicaer {#basicaer-1}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Most of the functionality in the `qiskit.providers.basicaer` module has been\n"
"replaced with the new\n"
"[`qiskit.providers.basic_provider`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/providers_basic_provider)\n"
"module, except for the `UnitarySimulatorPy` and `StatevectorSimulatorPy`\n"
"classes, which have been removed; their functionality was already contained in\n"
"the [`quantum_info`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/quantum_info) module.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The migration to the new paths is straightforward. You can replace most\n"
"classes in `qiskit.providers.basicaer` with their\n"
"[`qiskit.providers.basic_provider`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/providers_basic_provider)\n"
"counterpart (drop-in replacement). Note that the following classes have\n"
"new paths and names:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Removed                          | Alternative\n"
"---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------\n"
"`qiskit.providers.basicaer`                            |  [`qiskit.providers.basic_provider`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/providers_basic_provider)\n"
"`BasicAerProvider`             |  [`BasicProvider`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.basic_provider.BasicProvider)\n"
"`BasicAerJob`                       |  [`BasicProviderJob`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.basic_provider.BasicProviderJob)\n"
"`QasmSimulatorPy`               |  [`BasicSimulator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.basic_provider.BasicSimulator)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Global instances\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Be aware of any global instances when migrating to the new module. There is no replacement for\n"
"the `BasicAer` global instance that could be directly imported as `qiskit.BasicAer`. This means that\n"
" `from qiskit import BasicProvider` is no longer a valid import.\n"
"Instead, the provider class must be imported from its submodule and instantiated by the user:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The unitary and statevector simulators can be replaced with\n"
"different [`quantum_info`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/quantum_info) classes. This is not a\n"
"drop-in replacement, but the changes are minimal. See the following migration\n"
"examples:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Removed                          |   Alternative\n"
"---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------\n"
"`UnitarySimulatorPy`         |  [`quantum_info.Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator)\n"
"`StatevectorSimulatorPy` |  [`quantum_info.Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following examples show the migration paths of the `basicaer` "
"simulators.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"statevector\" label=\"Statevector simulator\" default>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    from qiskit import QuantumCircuit\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    qc = QuantumCircuit(3)\n"
"    qc.h(0)\n"
"    qc.h(1)\n"
"    qc.cx(1, 2)\n"
"    qc.measure_all()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Previous\n"
"    from qiskit import BasicAer\n"
"    backend = BasicAer.get_backend(\"statevector_simulator\")\n"
"    statevector = backend.run(qc).result().get_statevector()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Current\n"
"    qc.remove_final_measurements()  # no measurements allowed\n"
"    from qiskit.quantum_info import Statevector\n"
"    statevector = Statevector(qc)\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"unitary\" label=\"Unitary simulator\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    from qiskit import QuantumCircuit\n"
"    qc = QuantumCircuit(3)\n"
"    qc.h(0)\n"
"    qc.h(1)\n"
"    qc.cx(1, 2)\n"
"    qc.measure_all()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Previous\n"
"    from qiskit import BasicAer\n"
"    backend = BasicAer.get_backend(\"unitary_simulator\")\n"
"    result = backend.run(qc).result()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Current\n"
"    qc.remove_final_measurements()  # no measurements allowed\n"
"    from qiskit.quantum_info import Operator\n"
"    result = Operator(qc).data\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"qasm\" label=\"QASM simulator\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Previous\n"
"    from qiskit import BasicAer\n"
"    backend = BasicAer.get_backend(\"qasm_simulator\")\n"
"    result = backend.run(qc).result()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # One current option\n"
"    from qiskit.providers.basic_provider import BasicProvider\n"
"    backend = BasicProvider().get_backend(\"basic_simulator\")\n"
"    result = backend.run(qc).result()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Another current option is to specify it directly\n"
"    from qiskit.providers.basic_provider import BasicSimulator\n"
"    backend = BasicSimulator()\n"
"    result = backend.run(qc).result()\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"fake-backends-runtime\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "fake_provider {#fake-provider}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Most of the user-facing\n"
"`qiskit.providers.fake_provider` components have\n"
"been migrated to the `qiskit-ibm-runtime` Python package. This includes the\n"
"fake provider classes, all of the device-specific fake backends (such as\n"
"`FakeVigo`, `FakeNairobiV2`, and `FakeSherbrooke`), and the fake backend\n"
"base classes. Click through the following tabs to see the affected classes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"backends\" label=\"Fake Backends\" default>\n"
"      * Any class in `qiskit.providers.fake_provider.backends`\n"
"      * `fake_provider.fake_backend.FakeBackend`\n"
"      * `fake_provider.fake_backend.FakeBackendV2`\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"providers\" label=\"Fake Providers\">\n"
"      * `fake_provider.FakeProvider`\n"
"      * `fake_provider.FakeProviderForBackendV2`\n"
"      * `fake_provider.FakeProviderFactory`\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To migrate to the new path:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install `qiskit-ibm-runtime` `0.17.1` or later:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Replace instances of `qiskit.providers.fake_provider` in your code with\n"
"`qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider`. For example:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    # Old\n"
"    from qiskit.providers.fake_provider import FakeProvider\n"
"    backend1 = FakeProvider().get_backend(\"fake_ourense\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    from qiskit.providers.fake_provider import FakeSherbrooke\n"
"    backend2 = FakeSherbrooke()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Alternative\n"
"    from qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider import FakeProvider\n"
"    backend1 = FakeProvider().get_backend(\"fake_ourense\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    from qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider import FakeSherbrooke\n"
"    backend2 = FakeSherbrooke()\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fake backend base classes have also been migrated, but have some "
"differences in the import path:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Removed                          |   Alternative\n"
"---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------\n"
"`qiskit.providers.fake_provider.FakeQasmBackend`             |  `qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider.fake_qasm_backend.FakeQasmBackend`\n"
"`qiskit.providers.fake_provider.FakePulseBackend`             |  `qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider.fake_pulse_backend.FakePulseBackend`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you depend on fake backends for unit testing a downstream library and have conflicts with the\n"
"`qiskit-ibm-runtime` dependency, you can also find new Qiskit-native generic fake backend alternatives.\n"
"These include the following `BackendV1` classes (drop-in replacements):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`qiskit.providers.fake_provider.Fake5QV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.Fake5QV1)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`qiskit.providers.fake_provider.Fake20QV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.Fake20QV1)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`qiskit.providers.fake_provider.Fake7QPulseV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.Fake7QPulseV1)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`qiskit.providers.fake_provider.Fake27QPulseV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.Fake27QPulseV1)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`qiskit.providers.fake_provider.Fake127QPulseV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.Fake127QPulseV1)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is a configurable class that returns `BackendV2` instances:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* [`qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2)\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"fake_provider-special-testing-backends\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"fake_provider (special testing backends) {#fake-provider-special-testing-"
"backends}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fake backend classes for special testing purposes in\n"
"`qiskit.providers.fake_provider` have\n"
"**not** been migrated to `qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider`. The recommended\n"
"migration path is to use the new\n"
"[`GenericBackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2)\n"
"class to configure a backend with similar properties or to build a custom\n"
"target.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Removed                          |   Alternative\n"
"---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------\n"
"`fake_provider.FakeBackendV2` | [`fake_provider.GenericBackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2)\n"
"`fake_provider.FakeBackend5QV2` | [`fake_provider.GenericBackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2)\n"
"`fake_provider.FakeBackendV2LegacyQubitProps` | [`fake_provider.GenericBackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2)\n"
"`fake_provider.FakeBackendSimple` | [`fake_provider.GenericBackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2)\n"
"`fake_provider.ConfigurableFakeBackend` | [`fake_provider.GenericBackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example: Migrate to the new\n"
"[`GenericBackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.fake_provider.GenericBackendV2)\n"
"class:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"other-migration-tips\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Other migration tips {#other-migration-tips}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Importing from `qiskit.providers.aer` is no longer possible. Instead, import\n"
"from `qiskit_aer`, which is a drop-in replacement. To install `qiskit_aer`,\n"
"run:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install qiskit-aer\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Support for running pulse jobs on backends from\n"
"[`qiskit.providers.fake_provider`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/providers_fake_provider) has\n"
"been removed in Qiskit v1.0.  This is because Qiskit Aer removed its\n"
"simulation functionality for such jobs.  For low-level Hamiltonian-simulation\n"
"workloads, consider using a specialized library such as [Qiskit\n"
"Dynamics](https://qiskit-extensions.github.io/qiskit-dynamics/).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qiskit.pulse\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "qiskit.pulse {#qiskitpulse}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"ParametricPulse\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "ParametricPulse {#parametricpulse}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `qiskit.pulse.library.parametric_pulses.ParametricPulse` base class and\n"
"pulse library have been superseded by\n"
"[`qiskit.pulse.SymbolicPulse`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.SymbolicPulse)\n"
"and the corresponding pulse library. `SymbolicPulse` supports\n"
"[QPY](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qpy) serialization:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Removed                          |   Alternative\n"
"---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------\n"
"`pulse.library.parametric_pulses.ParametricPulse` | [`qiskit.pulse.SymbolicPulse`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.SymbolicPulse)\n"
"`pulse.library.parametric_pulses.Constant` |  [`pulse.library.symbolic_pulses.Constant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.Constant)\n"
"`pulse.library.parametric_pulses.Drag` |  [`pulse.library.symbolic_pulses.Drag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.Drag)\n"
"`pulse.library.parametric_pulses.Gaussian` |  [`pulse.library.symbolic_pulses.Gaussian`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.Gaussian)\n"
"`qiskit.pulse.library.parametric_pulses.GaussianSquare` |  [`pulse.library.symbolic_pulses.GaussianSquare`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.GaussianSquare)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"complex-val-amp\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Complex-valued amplitude {#complex-valued-amplitude}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Complex-valued pulse amplitude (`amp`) is replaced by an (`amp`,\n"
"`angle`) duo. This representation is more intuitive, especially for some\n"
"calibration tasks such as angle calibration:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"injecting-circuit-gate-operations\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Injecting circuit gate operations {#injecting-circuit-gate-operations}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Injecting circuit gate operations into the pulse builder context through\n"
"[`qiskit.pulse.builder.call`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/pulse#call) is no longer possible.\n"
"This removal affects input arguments of type `QuantumCircuit`, as well as the\n"
"following functions:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.builder.call_gate`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.builder.cx`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.builder.u1`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.builder.u2`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.builder.u3`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.builder.x`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you still want to inject backend-calibrated schedules, use the following\n"
"pattern instead of calling gate commands.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similarly, a [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) can\n"
"be injected in the builder context by manually transpiling and scheduling the\n"
"object.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We recommend writing a minimum pulse program with the builder and attaching it to\n"
"`QuantumCircuit` through the\n"
"[`QuantumCircuit.add_calibration`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#add_calibration)\n"
"method as a microcode of a gate instruction, rather than writing the entire\n"
"program with the pulse model.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"builder.build\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "builder.build {#builderbuild}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following arguments in `qiskit.pulse.builder.build` have been removed with\n"
"no alternative.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`default_transpiler_settings`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`default_circuit_scheduler_settings`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "These functions have also been removed:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.builder.active_transpiler_settings`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.builder.active_circuit_scheduler_settings`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.builder.transpiler_settings`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.builder.circuit_scheduler_settings`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is because it's no longer possible to inject circuit objects into the\n"
"builder context (see [Injecting circuit gate\n"
"operations](#injecting-circuit-gate-operations)); these settings were for\n"
"converting injected objects into pulse representations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"pulse.library\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "library {#library}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The discrete pulse library has been removed from the code base. This "
"includes:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.constant`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.zero`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.square`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.sawtooth`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.triangle`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.cos`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.sin`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.gaussian`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.gaussian_deriv`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.sech`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.sech_deriv`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.gaussian_square`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit.pulse.library.drag`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Instead, use the corresponding\n"
"[`qiskit.pulse.SymbolicPulse`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.SymbolicPulse),\n"
"with\n"
"[`SymbolicPulse.get_waveform()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.SymbolicPulse#get_waveform).\n"
"For example, instead of `pulse.gaussian(100,0.5,10)`, use\n"
"`pulse.Gaussian(100,0.5,10).get_waveform()`. Note that the phase of both\n"
"[`Sawtooth`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.Sawtooth) and\n"
"[`Square`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.Square) is defined such\n"
"that a phase of `2\\\\pi` shifts by a full cycle, contrary to the discrete\n"
"counterpart. Also note that complex amplitudes are no longer supported in\n"
"the symbolic pulse library; use `float`, `amp`, and  `angle` instead.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"ScalableSymbolicPulse\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "ScalableSymbolicPulse {#scalablesymbolicpulse}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is no longer possible to load library `qiskit.pulse.ScalableSymbolicPulse`\n"
"objects with a complex `amp` parameter from version 5 or earlier qpy files\n"
"(Qiskit Terra < 0.23.0). No migration action is required, as complex `amp` will\n"
"automatically be converted to `float` (`amp`, `angle`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This change applies to these pulses:\n"
"* [`qiskit.pulse.Constant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.Constant)\n"
"* [`qiskit.pulse.Drag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.Drag)\n"
"* [`qiskit.pulse.Gaussian`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.Gaussian)\n"
"* [`qiskit.pulse.GaussianSquare`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.pulse.library.GaussianSquare)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qiskit.qasm\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "qiskit.qasm {#qiskitqasm}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The legacy OpenQASM 2 parser module previously in `qiskit.qasm` has\n"
"been superseded by the [`qiskit.qasm2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qasm2) module, which\n"
"provides a faster and more accurate parser for OpenQASM 2. The high level\n"
"`QuantumCircuit` methods\n"
"[`from_qasm_file()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#from_qasm_file)\n"
"and\n"
"[`from_qasm_str()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#from_qasm_str)\n"
"remain the same, but will use the new parser internally. However, the public\n"
"interface for the `qasm2` module is not the same. While the `qiskit.qasm`\n"
"module provided an interface to an abstract syntax tree returned by the `ply`\n"
"parser library, `qiskit.qasm2` does not expose the AST or any lower level\n"
"implementation details about the parser. It instead takes OpenQASM 2 input and\n"
"outputs a [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) object.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For example, if you were previously running something like this:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Replace it with the following:\n"
msgstr ""

